Because forwarding all headers disables header-based cache key optimization — CloudFront can't cache anything when every possible request header variation creates a separate cache entry. We only need `Authorization` (for Bearer tokens) and `Content-Type` (for JSON parsing) to reach the backend; letting extra browser headers like `User-Agent` or `Accept-Language` vary the cache key would blow up the cache footprint with no benefit.

