## 1. Yes — Cache Policy + Origin Request Policy decouples them

The legacy `ForwardedValues` API bundled "what goes into the cache key" and "what gets forwarded to the origin" into one opaque blob. Since ~2020, **Cache Policies** control the cache key, and **Origin Request Policies** control what gets forwarded. They're attached independently to the same cache behavior.

> *"Origin request policies are separate from cache policies, which control the cache key. This way, you can receive additional information at the origin and also maintain a good cache hit ratio."*
